load @term/seed/code/type/term
  find term

# The identity type, the observational equality the kernel computes with. For two values of one type it is the type of
# proofs that they are equal. The intensional core (reflexivity and the J eliminator) is made OBSERVATIONAL by adding
# computing extensionality rules, the committed choice over both bare intensional equality (too weak, no funext) and
# full univalence (too strong, undecidable to teach and unneeded for a programming language). Its rules in full.

# FORMATION: from a type A and two values of A, form the identity type, the type of equality proofs between them.
form identity-type
  link space, like term
  link left, like term
  link right, like term

# INTRODUCTION: reflexivity. Every value is equal to itself, witnessed by the canonical proof refl, the only direct way
# to build an equality.
form reflexivity
  link value, like term

# ELIMINATION (J): to prove a property holds along any equality proof, it suffices to prove it at reflexivity. The J
# rule is path induction, and every theorem about equality (symmetry, transitivity, congruence, transport) is derived
# from it.
form path-induction
  link proof, like term
  link motive, like term

# COMPUTATION at a function type (function extensionality, COMPUTED): the identity at a pi type reduces to the pointwise
# identity (two functions are equal exactly when they agree at every argument), so funext is the identity function, not
# a postulate. This is the observational extension's defining rule.
form function-extensionality
  link space, like term

# COMPUTATION at a pair type (pair extensionality): the identity at a sigma reduces componentwise (a pair of equality
# proofs), via transport in the dependent case. Together with funext this makes equality extensional while keeping
# type-checking decidable.
form pair-extensionality
  link space, like term

# TRANSPORT: an equality proof between two values carries any structure indexed by the first to the same structure
# indexed by the second, the dependent companion of J, the operation that moves a value along an equality.
form transport
  link proof, like term
  link family, like term
